Quotapool
============

This project is two layers, and they have different origins. Saying so at the
top level matters: the derivation was previously recorded only in
`vendor/teamclaude/VENDOR-NOTICE.md`, which nobody landing on the repository
would see.


Data plane — a fork
-------------------

`vendor/teamclaude/` is derived from **TeamClaude**:

    @karpeleslab/teamclaude 1.1.11
    https://github.com/KarpelesLab/teamclaude
    Copyright (c) 2026 KarpelesLab
    MIT License — retained verbatim in vendor/teamclaude/LICENSE

Obtained from the npm registry on 2026-07-28. The upstream tarball's SHA-256 and
npm integrity hash are recorded in `vendor/teamclaude/VENDOR-NOTICE.md`, along
with a per-item list of what was changed.

TeamClaude continues to own OAuth refresh, the MITM proxy, SSE forwarding, the
request-body account UUID rewrite, and quota-rejection retry. The fork does not
claim upstream endorsement.

In broad terms the fork:

- delegates account selection to a loopback-only Fleet coordinator before an
  upstream request begins, and fails closed if that coordinator is unreachable;
- accepts subscription OAuth accounts only, binds to loopback, and disables
  keep-warm and self-update;
- refuses sx.org egress routing outright (see "Deliberate omissions" below).


Control plane — original
------------------------

`src/claude_fleet/`, `scripts/`, `bin/`, `tests/` and the packaging are original
work under the MIT licence in `LICENSE`.


Not affiliated with Anthropic
-----------------------------

Quotapool is not an Anthropic product and carries no Anthropic endorsement.
"Claude" and "Claude Code" are Anthropic's. This is a self-hosted local tool that
runs on your own machine, holds your own credentials, and routes your own
requests to subscriptions you hold yourself. It is not a hosted service, it does
not offer sign-in to anyone, and it never routes requests on behalf of a third
party.


Deliberate omissions
--------------------

Several things upstream offers are removed rather than merely unused, and they
are a product position rather than an unfinished feature:

- **No API keys and no usage credits.** Nothing here can create spend outside a
  subscription you already pay for.
- **No third-party upstreams.** Upstream supports routing to Anthropic-compatible
  APIs as a fallback; that is removed.
- **No IP evasion.** Upstream can provision a residential proxy to work around
  IP-based rate limits. That path is refused at startup and again on every
  config reload.

Not another name
----------------

`claude-fleet` on npm is an unrelated project by a different author. There is no
shared code, history, or affiliation.
